  "question": {
    "text": "When 2 litre of ideal gas expands isothermally into vacuum to a total volume of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> litre, the change in internal energy is _____&nbsp;J. (Nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For ideal gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and for isothermal process, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,<br />Also&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi>ext</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, thus work done in vacuum is also zero. Internal energy is a fuction of temperature."
  }
